priors into a massive MLP.

204
00:09:38,950 --> 00:09:43,420
But in some sense that's
just about efficiency.

205
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:47,180
So a metaphor we found useful,
which is also biological,

206
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:49,680
is that language models
should be thought of as grown,

207
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:52,418
not built. You start with this
randomly initialized thing

208
00:09:52,418 --> 00:09:54,210
and architecture, which
is like a scaffold.

209
00:09:54,210 --> 00:09:57,930
You like give it some data,
maybe that's like a nutrient.

210
00:09:57,930 --> 00:10:01,500
And then the loss is like the
sun and it grows towards that.

211
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:03,770
And so you get this
organic thing which

212
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:06,050
has been made by the end of it.

213
00:10:06,050 --> 00:10:09,950

214
00:10:09,950 --> 00:10:12,170
But the way that it
grew, you don't really

215
00:10:12,170 --> 00:10:15,000
have any access to it.

216
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,263
The scaffold you have access to.

217
00:10:17,263 --> 00:10:18,680
But that's like
looking at a model

218
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:21,590
